  "summary": "Architecture course clips now draw every person, device, furniture item, machine, vehicle and building component only from the handcrafted staffage archive.\n- **Bridge:** a TS cast exporter (schema; elevation, plan and front views; theme and transport; 600-frame cap; content-keyed cache) and a Python staffage, staffage_motion, fitted_staffage and pendant_lamp API with a lazy, bounded parser.\n- **New handcrafted assets:** humans, a new appliances category, machinery for the heat-pump and DEC hardware, objects, front and plan views. The catalog check passes 144/144.\n- **Deleted:** silhouettes, person, object and lamp glyphs, radiator(), the activity SVGs and every primitive-built device.\n- **Thermal rule:** energy and optimization comfort clips use the animated thermal staffage views.\n- **Guard:** the `staffage_only` test enforces the rule.\n- **Verification:** visuals Python tests (including integration and the guard) pass, staffage vitest 994 passed, and the changed scenes were rendered and inspected.\n- **Known infra leftovers:** repo dependencies ensure refuses, optimization has a pre-existing $schema assertion failure, and the long BIM suites are not fully run.\nThe full summary is in summary.md in the ticket folder.",
